Subject: [PATCH] mgmtd: link management CLI archive before libfrr

libmgmt_be_nb contains RIP/RIPng CLI callbacks referencing if_rmap and
distribute functions in libfrr. With static archives, placing libfrr first
leaves these references unresolved because GNU ld has already scanned it.

Use the dependency order present in upstream mgmtd/subdir.am. Keep all
protocol daemons enabled and retain the pinned FRR 10.4.1 sources.

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/FRRouting/frr/blob/master/mgmtd/subdir.am]

--- a/mgmtd/subdir.am
+++ b/mgmtd/subdir.am
@@ -66,8 +66,7 @@
 	yang/ietf/ietf-netconf-with-defaults.yang.c \
 	# nothing
 mgmtd_mgmtd_CFLAGS = $(AM_CFLAGS) -I ./
-mgmtd_mgmtd_LDADD = mgmtd/libmgmtd.a lib/libfrr.la $(LIBCAP) $(LIBM) $(LIBYANG_LIBS) $(UST_LIBS)
-mgmtd_mgmtd_LDADD += mgmtd/libmgmt_be_nb.la
+mgmtd_mgmtd_LDADD = mgmtd/libmgmtd.a mgmtd/libmgmt_be_nb.la lib/libfrr.la $(LIBCAP) $(LIBM) $(LIBYANG_LIBS) $(UST_LIBS)
 
 
 if STATICD
